उद्-√ 1. द्युत् P. Ved. (impf. -अद्यौत्) Ā. -द्योतते, to blaze up, shine, shine forth, RV. iii, 5, 9; Hariv.;
 Caus. P. -द्योतयति, to cause to shine or shine forth, Prab.; Ragh. :
Intens. Ved. (Subj. -द॑विद्युतत्) to shine intensely, RV. vi, 16, 45.

उद्-√ या P. -याति, to rise (as the sun), RV. x, 37, 3;
to go out or away, start from, ŚBr. xiv, 5, 4, 1; Ragh.;
to raise one's self, rise, Gīt.; Kathās.;
to rise, originate from, Rājat.; Naiṣ.;
to excel, surpass (acc.), MārkP.

उद्-√ यम् P. -यच्छति (aor. -अयान्, RV. vi, 71, 5), Ā. (if the result of the action returns to the agent, Pāṇ. i, 3, 75) -यच्छते (aor. -अयंस्त and -यमिष्ट);
 Subj. -यंसते, RV. i, 143, 7;
 (inf. -य॑मम्, MaitrS. ii, 4, 3) to lift up, raise, RV. v, 32, 7; vi, 71, 1 & 5; AV.; AitBr.; ŚBr.; Lāṭy.; Śak. &c.;
to raise, set up, elevate;
to put up or higher, carry or bring upwards, RV. iv, 53, 1; i, 143, 7; TS.; ŚBr.; KātyŚr. &c.;
to hold out, present, offer (a sacrifice to gods, or any other thing to men), RV.; AV.; TS.; MBh.; BhP.; R. &c.;
to shake up, rouse, RV. i, 10, 1; i, 56, 1; x, 119, 2; AV. xiv, 1, 59;
to raise (one's voice, or rays, or light), RV.;
to undertake, commence;
to be diligent, strive after (only P., e.g. उद्यच्छति चिकित्सां वैद्यः, ‘the physician strives after the science of medicine’, Kāś. on Pāṇ. i, 3, 75; with dat. or acc. or without any object), MBh.; Hariv.; Ragh.; Kathās.; Rājat. &c.;
to rein, curb;
to guide, MBh.;
to keep away or off, restrain, check, TS. vi, 3, 4, 6; TBr. iii, 3, 1, 3 :
Intens. -यम्यमीति, to raise, stretch out (the arms), RV. i, 95, 7.

उद्-√ 2. यु P. Ā. -यौति, (1. pl. -युवामहे) to draw up or upwards, RV. vi, 57, 6; TS. ii, 6, 5, 5;
to join, mix;
to confound.

1. उद्-√ युज् P. Ā. -युनक्ति, -युङ्क्ते (inf. -युजे॑, AV.) to join, be in contact with, AV. vi, 70, 2;
to get off or away, go away, ŚBr. iv, 1, 5, 7; Lāṭy.;
to go near, undergo, prepare;
to make efforts, be active, MBh.; Kathās.; Daś. :
Caus. -योजयति, to excite, incite, make active or quick, stimulate to exertion, MBh.; Hariv.; R.
